# Frontend Development Rules

## Styling Guidelines

- Use Tailwind CSS predefined variables: `bg-primary`, `text-primary`, `border-primary`, etc.
- check `/lib/theme.css` for the color variables and `tailwind.config.js` for the color mapping
- Avoid custom CSS variables like `--shiplight-bg-primary`, `--shiplight-text-primary`, etc.
- Prefer Mantine components as they are already themed
- Minimize custom styles - only add colors when explicitly needed

## Component Development

- Always check `src/components/common` directory first when implementing features
- Create components in `src/components/common` for:
  - Common capabilities
  - Mantine components requiring extensive custom styles/behaviors
- Prioritize reusing existing components over duplicate implementations

## Technical Stack

- Tailwind CSS for styling
- Mantine for UI components
- Follow component-based development principles
- Maintain code consistency and simplicity
